  "rationale": "Direct-match melanoma candidates are present (e.g., PGS000079, PGS000118, PGS000732, PGS000743, PGS000766, PGS000790, PGS001304, PGS002246/PGS002247, etc.). PGS000079 is best supported in the visible context because it targets an endpoint tightly aligned to the target trait (phenotyping_reported: incident melanoma; trait_reported/efo: melanoma), is evaluated in European ancestry, and has large validation (n=392,803) with consistent risk signal (C-index 0.663; HR per SD 1.43 [1.36–1.49]) under a broadly comparable covariate set (age/sex/PCs/array plus UV-related factors, which are epidemiologic rather than disease-leakage variables). Competing melanoma models either have substantially smaller validation (e.g., PGS000743/744/745), are specialized (familial/non-carrier subgroup in PGS000813; childhood cancer survivor risk in PGS005208), are framework-style pan-trait scores with only modest discrimination (e.g., snpnet PGS001304), or are essentially variants/weight re-expressions of the same underlying model family (PGS000790), leaving PGS000079 as the most coherent, broadly supported direct-match choice. Limitation: most candidates (including PGS000079) report only full-model discrimination metrics rather than explicit PRS-only AUROC/R2, so cross-model comparability and isolation of the PRS contribution remain uncertain, lowering confidence from High to Moderate."
}

