  "rationale": "Direct-match candidates to uterine cancer are present, including (i) PGS001795 with trait_reported/phenotyping_reported both “Uterine cancer” (closest endpoint fidelity to the target), and (ii) PGS000541/PGS000542 with trait_efo “uterine cancer” but phenotyping_reported “Malignant neoplasm of uterus” (also direct). PGS001795 is preferred because it is the only candidate whose reported trait and endpoint explicitly match “Uterine cancer” and it provides PRS-comparable metrics (pgs_only_r2=0.001948; auc field present at 0.66) with basic covariates (sex/age/PCs). Main limitation: evidence remains mixed because other direct uterine-cancer-labeled scores (PGS000541/PGS000542) report effect sizes (OR≈1.30 per SD; top 1% ORs) but have lower full-model AUROC (~0.57), and endometrial-cancer models (a dominant uterine subtype per provided domain knowledge) show much higher full-model AUROC but are not exact-label uterine cancer endpoints; additionally, most AUCs shown are full-model or not clearly PRS-only, reducing comparability and preventing a high-confidence choice."
}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_SUB_OPTIMAL","best_model_id":"PGS000054","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"All 5 candidates are direct matches at the concept level (trait_efo = late-onset Alzheimer's disease). Endpoint fidelity is strongest for models explicitly targeting late-onset AD/LOAD (PGS000053, PGS000054, PGS000334, PGS004918); PGS002289 is concept-aligned but its phenotyping_reported reflects a cognition-by-age interaction rather than a direct AD diagnosis endpoint, making it a weaker direct-match endpoint.

Among the endpoint-faithful candidates, only PGS000053/PGS000054 report a PRS-comparable effect size (OR per SD). PGS000054 shows a stronger OR (1.73, 95% CI 1.57–1.93) than PGS000053 (OR 1.29, 95% CI 1.21–1.37), which is supportive evidence of stronger PRS discrimination per the provided guidance. The remaining candidates provide either only full-model AUROC with small n and unknown covariates (PGS004918; AUROC 0.731, n=136; not interpretable as PRS-only) or an R² value reported under other_metrics with unknown covariates (PGS000334; R²=0.191) that is hard to interpret as PRS-only and is flagged by the domain guidance as potentially non-comparable/suspect for simple C+T in a complex trait.

Limitation: PGS000054 is evaluated in AMR (Hispanic/Latin American) rather than EUR, while several alternatives are EUR-evaluated; because the deployment ancestry is not specified and no PRS-only AUC/R² is available for any candidate, the ranking remains uncertain and thus sub-optimal overall despite preferring the strongest available per-SD effect size among direct endpoint matches."}

