  "rationale": "All three candidates are direct matches under the broad target concept of blood coagulation disease, but they represent different endpoints: PGS001033 is explicitly mapped to the target EFO (“blood coagulation disease”) with phenotyping_reported as “TTE other coagulation defects,” while PGS001826 and PGS002034 target a narrower congenital clotting-factor deficiency EFO (vitamin K–dependent factors) and thus are less well-aligned to the broad umbrella trait. PGS001033 also provides the most explicit PRS-comparable performance evidence in the context (PGS-only AUROC and PGS R2 reported), whereas the two congenital-deficiency models report only partial correlation and no AUROC/R2. However, the evidence remains limited and conflicting in quality signals: PGS001033 comes from a pan-trait sparse UKB framework paper (a known weakness signal in the provided domain knowledge) and is extremely sparse (1 variant), while the other two are from a portability framework and are near-identical siblings with slightly better partial-r but for a narrower phenotype. Given these tradeoffs and lack of a clearly strong disease-focused, endpoint-faithful alternative, the best available direct-match is PGS001033 but with low confidence."
